 descriptions={
 1:'''**Figure 1. Study overview.** (A) Measured ST and coordinates support frozen reconstruction of hidden expression; H&E is optional. (B) Distributed anchors (teal) with unmeasured locations (gray). (C) A contiguous forbidden region (purple), with anchors outside it. Coordinates and20%anchor counts here are synthetic, seed17; this is a technical schematic, not a biological result. No patient n, metric or uncertainty estimate applies.''',
 2:'''**Figure 2. Development reconstruction.** TENX99, one primary development patient, original50genes. Panels A/C show V1 distributed sampling; B/D show the earlier C5block protocol (V2). A/B: median gene Pearson; C/D: mean gene MSE in C0normalized log1p units. Each point is the mean of3frozen masks at5%,10%,20%,40%,60%,80%coverage. Gray=ResNet18 H&E, teal=validation-selected interpolation, brown=fixed fusion. Lines connect tested settings; no confidence intervals. The block protocol differs from C9/C10fixed40%forbidden-region V2. Fusion can improve r while worsening MSE relative to ST.''',
 3:'''**Figure 3. Geometry, distance and development reliability.** TENX99, one development patient,50genes. (A) Selected ST-only error at20%coverage by nearest-anchor distance bin, V1andC5block V2. Means over masks; occupied bins only. (B) Secondary C6open interpolation-only comparison: random A0mean over10seeds versus deterministic spatialFPS A1 at5/10/20/40%; this is not evidence of general sampling optimality. (C/D) Frozen C5ResNet18fusion,20%,replicate0,first original panel gene FOXA1, random/block masks. Hidden-location absolute errors are colored in C0units; observed anchors are teal. Shared color maximum is the98thpercentile across all three prespecified map regimes, including capture-window source data; values above it saturate. No spots are deleted. Full values/barcodes/sourcepredictionhashes are in Fig3_map_source.csv. No biological annotations or outcome-based gene selection. The spatial panels have an equal physical aspect ratio.''',
 4:'''**Figure 4. HER2ST transportability development.** Eight patients, exact common40-gene intersection. A/C V1 and B/D V2 at20%random coverage. A/B median gene Pearson; C/D mean gene MSE in common C0normalized units (log axis). Dots represent patients after averaging seeds and geometries; connected markers are medians across patients. Gray=T0zero-shot, brown=T1calibrated. H&E,STandfixed fusion are shown separately. T0exactlyreplays C7;T1belongs to C8transportability development and is not fresh external validation. Affine interpolation maps back to the same common-unit prediction, so calibration is not a unique STinterpolation gain. No error bars or inferential tests.''',
 5:'''**Figure 5. Fresh Wu validation.** Three held-out local Wu patients,50genes, after separately locked calibration inthree other patients. (A)20%V1, dots=patients, horizontalbars=median patient Pearson. (B)10/20/40%V1correlation; (C)MSE in common C0units, logarithmicaxis. Curves show patient medians. (D)Paired patient correlation effects at20%V1; horizontalbars=median paired effect, which need not equal the difference of cohort medians. (E)Paired ST-only V1/V2patient scores at20%. (F)ST-only distance-bin MSE at20%, patient means over seeds/equal geometries then cohort median of available patients. M0=H&E,M1=ST,M3=fixed0.2image fusion. Equivalent M2is omitted from plottedduplicatecurves; no harmonization gain is claimed. Public images contain15/25nativepixels per112µmpatch. No confidence intervals; three patients are the biological units.''',
 6:'''**Figure 6. Second fresh replication.** Twenty-two Bassiouni patients, one first section each,50genes; all are evaluation patients with no C10fitting. Panels match Figure5: A20%V1patientcorrelations; B/Ccoveragecorrelation/error; DpairedSTandfusioneffects; EpairedV1/V2; Fdistance-binMSE. Random seeds are averaged within geometry and geometries equally within patients; bars/curves are patient medians. M3transports the already-frozen Wu scaler and0.2imageweight. Image resolution is24–29nativepixels per112µmpatch. The cohort supports sparse ST, but fixedfusion lacks reproducible error benefit. Distance curves are descriptive and not universally monotonic; variable support and location composition prohibit a universal cutoff.''',
 7:'''**Figure 7. Cross-cohort synthesis without pooling panels.** Columns: developmentprimaryn=1,HER2STzero-shotn=8,HER2STcalibratedn=8,Wufreshn=3,Bassiounifreshn=22. The two HER2STcolumns reuse the same patients, not independent cohorts. Development/Wu/Bassiouni use50genes;HER2STuses40. A–E:20%V1pairedpatient effects, dots=patients,bars=median; ST−H&E andfusion−ST. F–J: individualpatientSTcorrelationcurves at10/20/40%V1. Axes remain cohort-specific and no pooled scalar is computed. Development and calibration-development are distinguished from fresh validation. No confidence intervals or significance tests.'''}
