 text='# Figure legends\n\nAll figures are descriptive. MSE/MAE use common C0 training-normalized log1p count units. Patient is the biological unit; mask/model seeds quantify algorithmic variation. No error bars are shown and none should be interpreted as confidence intervals. For distance panels, bins are [0,150),[150,300),[300,600),[600,1200),[1200,2400),[2400,infinity)µm; only occupied bins contribute, and available patient counts can change across bins. Bin Pearson requires20locations perrun; errors retain sparsebins. Exact run-level counts and metrics are in Supplementary Table7.\n\n'
